    <exercises>
        <title>5.3: Uses of Radioactive Materials</title>

        <exercise>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Why can a radioactive tracer be useful in medicine even when
                    only a small amount is administered?
                </p>
            </statement>

            <answer>
                <p>
                    Its radiation can be detected from outside the body,
                    allowing the location or movement of the tracer to be
                    followed.
                </p>
            </answer>
        </exercise>

        <exercise>
