        <exercise>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    In nuclear fission, why can one fission event lead to
                    additional fission events?
                </p>
            </statement>

            <answer>
                <p>
                    Fission can release neutrons that strike other fissile
                    nuclei, producing a chain reaction.
                </p>
            </answer>
        </exercise>

